.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Forest topology in a conventional mesh format\&. 

A typical workflow starts with \fBp8est_mesh_params_init\fP to initialize a \fBp8est_mesh_params_t\fP, followed by eventual user-dependent changes to the parameters\&.
.PP
Next a \fBp8est_mesh_t\fP is created with \fBp8est_mesh_new_params\fP\&.
.PP
Now, the user can create a \fBp8est_mesh_face_neighbor_t\fP with \fBp8est_mesh_face_neighbor_init\fP and loop over a quadrants face neighbors by repeated calls to \fBp8est_mesh_face_neighbor_next\fP\&.
.PP
Once done, the mesh has to be destroyed with \fBp8est_mesh_destroy\fP\&. 
.SH "Function Documentation"
