.SS "void p8est_mesh_params_init (\fBp8est_mesh_params_t\fP * params)"

.PP
Initialize a default \fBp8est_mesh_params_t\fP structure\&. The parameters are set to create the most basic mesh structure, without tree index and level lists and considering only face connections\&. 
.SS "\fBp8est_quadrant_t\fP* p8est_mesh_quadrant_cumulative (\fBp8est_t\fP * p8est, \fBp8est_mesh_t\fP * mesh, \fBp4est_locidx_t\fP cumulative_id, \fBp4est_topidx_t\fP * which_tree, \fBp4est_locidx_t\fP * quadrant_id)"

.PP
Find a quadrant based on its cumulative number in the local forest\&. If the quad_to_tree field of the mesh structure exists, this is O(1)\&. Otherwise, we perform a binary search over the processor-local trees\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fI\fBp8est\fP\fP Forest to be worked with\&. 
.br
\fImesh\fP A mesh derived from the forest\&. 
.br
\fIcumulative_id\fP Cumulative index over all trees of quadrant\&. Must refer to a local (non-ghost) quadrant\&. 
.br
\fIwhich_tree\fP If not NULL, the input value can be -1 or an initial guess for the quadrant's tree and output is the tree of returned quadrant\&. 
.br
\fIquadrant_id\fP If not NULL, the number of quadrant in tree\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The identified quadrant\&. 
.RE
.PP

